  "recovery": {
    "headline": "By 2025, five of the eight blocked groups were back to at least 90 percent of their 2017\u201319 sales to China (Barley, Shellfish, Beef, Cotton and Copper ores). Wine and drinks and Coal were only part of the way back. Timber logs were still well short.",
    "means": "\u201cBack\u201d means 2025 sales reached at least 90 percent of the 2017\u201319 average. During the blocked years, recorded sales were $41.2 billion below that old average. Coal is most of it, about $26.5 billion. A comparison with goods that were not blocked is in the method note. It also moves for wool, which was not blocked, so these pages use the recorded average.",
    "wheat": "China's wheat purchases rose from $103 million in 2019 to $3.2 billion in 2023, while barley was blocked. Wheat is not used as a stand-in for a normal year.",
